00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:47.160
<v Sarah>Because everyone kept trying to tell me, oh, you know, you really hate this job. And you just don't know that you hate it. But I couldn't feel that I hated it. I called my sort of like closest friend and said, do you think it's stupid that I'm doing this? Like I don't feel like I don't like this job. I feel like I like it. I get up in the morning and I go to it and I don't mind. And he was like, well, if you feel like you like it, then you probably do. That was sort of a ramble. But I guess what I'm trying to say is there were really, really crappy things about it, but it was so far from the worst job that I've ever had.
<v Sarah>因为每个人都一直在试图告诉我，哦，你知道，你其实很讨厌这份工作。你只是不知道自己讨厌它。但我感觉不到自己讨厌它。我打电话给我最亲近的朋友说，我做这个是不是很傻？我觉得我不讨厌这份工作。我觉得我喜欢它。我早上起床去上班，我不介意。他说，好吧，如果你觉得你喜欢它，那你就可能真的喜欢。我有点语无伦次了。但我想说的是，这份工作确实有很多糟糕的地方，但它远非我做过最烂的工作。

