00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:41.580
<v Ira Glass>Last summer, reporter and radio producer Sandy Tolan was going to do a story about the sex industry from the worker's prospective, with a woman named Susan Walsh. Walsh was an aspiring writer who worked in go-go bars in New Jersey to support her son. And then a week or so before they were going to start work on their documentary, Susan Walsh disappeared.
<v Ira Glass>去年夏天，记者兼广播制作人桑迪·托兰打算以工人的视角做一个关于性产业的报道，对象是一位名叫苏珊·沃尔什的女性。沃尔什是一位有抱负的作家，在新泽西州的舞厅工作以抚养儿子。而在他们准备开始拍摄纪录片前一周左右，苏珊·沃尔什失踪了。

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:57.060
<v Ira Glass>On July 16, she left her home in Nutley, New Jersey, to make a call at a pay phone on the corner. She didn't have a phone at home. She left her wallet, her keys, and her beeper behind. She told her son that she would be right back, and she never came back. Everybody close to her assumes that she's dead.
<v Ira Glass>7月16日，她离开新泽西州纳特利的家，去街角的公用电话打了个电话。她家里没有电话。她把钱包、钥匙和传呼机都留下了。她告诉儿子她马上回来，但她再也没回来。她身边的人都认为她已经遇害了。

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:07.830
<v Ira Glass>So Sandy Tolan decided to set out on a different story. To try to understand what her life was like in the go-go bars of Jersey. And to understand what might have led to her life coming apart.
<v Ira Glass>于是桑迪·托兰决定换一个故事。试图了解她在新泽西舞厅的生活是怎样的。以及了解是什么导致了她生活的崩溃。

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:18.830
