00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:37.910
<v Sandy Tolan>My first stop is at The Village Voice , where my old friend, James Ridgeway, works as a political correspondent. Jim had suggested Susan Walsh and I work together. She was the researcher for his new book, Red Light: Inside the Sex Industry, which tells the story from the point of view of the workers, strippers, street walkers, call girls, and porn actors.
<v Sandy Tolan>我的第一站是《乡村之声》，我的老朋友詹姆斯·里奇韦在那里担任政治通讯员。吉姆建议我和苏珊·沃尔什合作。她是吉姆新书《红灯：性产业内幕》的研究员，这本书从舞女、站街女、应召女郎和色情演员等从业者的角度讲述了性产业的故事。

00:06:37.910 --> 00:07:05.670
<v James Ridgeway>I first met Susan Walsh in the offices of Screw magazine when I was working on a book about the sex industry. And I went to see Al Goldstein, who was the editor. And as I was talking to him, I was complaining about how I couldn't get anywhere in this whole business. And asked him if he could give me some advice. And he said, well, you know, there's this woman that comes in here every so often and she writes for us and she'd be really good because she really knows this stuff.
<v James Ridgeway>我第一次见到苏珊·沃尔什是在《螺丝》杂志的办公室，当时我正在写一本关于性产业的书。我去见主编阿尔·戈德斯坦。我在和他交谈时，抱怨自己在这个行业里寸步难行，并请他给我一些建议。他说，好吧，你知道，有个女人经常来这里，她为我们写稿，她会非常出色，因为她真的很了解这些东西。

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:29.990
<v James Ridgeway>And at that point, for some reason, this woman suddenly appeared and she had this kind of long, blonde hair. It was kind of flying in the wind. And she had this motorcycle jacket and she's real skinny and awkward looking. She hardly looked like somebody you'd think was a striptease dancer, or go-go dancer. She looked like kind of a college kid. Only as I later learned that Susan was in her 30s.
<v James Ridgeway>就在那时，不知何故，这个女人突然出现了，她留着一头长长的金发。在风中飘扬。她穿着一件摩托夹克，人非常瘦，看起来有些笨拙。她看起来一点也不像你会认为的脱衣舞女或舞女。她看起来就像个大学生。直到后来我才知道，苏珊已经30多岁了。

