<v Sandy Tolan>Susan longed to be a full-time writer. Jim got her to write a few pieces on go-go for the Voice . He set her up with a couple of film and radio gigs, but dancing paid the bills. She'd work six days a week sometimes, two shifts a day, just barely making it.
