<v David>Oh, Lucky & Wild. That's a great two-player game.
<v David>哦，《幸运与狂野》。那是个很棒的双人游戏。

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:28.860
<v Sandy Tolan>Martha watches David run off, dashing between video games. She's glad he's got something else to do besides think about his mother. She says he's blocking his feelings, not wanting to confront the possibilities.
<v Sandy Tolan>玛莎看着大卫跑开，穿梭在电子游戏机之间。她很高兴他除了想念母亲之外还有别的事可做。她说他在封闭自己的感受，不想面对现实的可能性。

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:45.470
<v Martha>I hope Suzy is still alive, but it's the not knowing that is so horrible. But it's also what would be worse is knowing that she isn't with us anymore. I'm just crazy inside. I feel as though I'm broken apart.
<v Martha>我希望苏西还活着，但这种未知的状态太可怕了。更糟糕的是知道她已经不在我们身边了。我内心都要疯了。我觉得自己整个人都破碎了。

00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:55.500
<v Sandy Tolan>This is all so unlike Susan, her mom says. She would never leave David like this. Then Martha pauses a moment. She has something she wants to say. She stares at my microphone.
<v Sandy Tolan>这一切太不像苏珊了，她妈妈说。她绝不会就这样丢下大卫。然后玛莎停顿了一会儿。她有话想说。她盯着我的麦克风。

00:15:55.500 --> 00:16:23.770
<v Martha>Hi, Suzy, this is mom. If you're listening or if you hear about this, I want to give a message to you. I love you very, very much. More than anybody in the world. And I just want to see you again. And please, take good care of yourself wherever you are and know that you're loved and missed so much by everybody. I love you.
<v Martha>嗨，苏西，我是妈妈。如果你正在听或者听说这件事，我想给你留个口信。我爱你，非常非常多。比世界上任何人都多。我只是想再见你一面。无论你在哪里，请照顾好自己，要知道每个人都非常爱你和想念你。我爱你。

00:16:23.770 --> 00:16:45.470
<v Sandy Tolan>Late October, three and a half months now since Susan disappeared. Jill Morley and I are in Midtown, Manhattan. We're paying a visit on Susan's therapist, Mary Nolan, who works a lot with go-go girls and prostitutes. We're trying to make sense of something. By all accounts, Susan had a lot going for her outside of go-go, and she wasn't making much money dancing, yet she kept doing it.
<v Sandy Tolan>十月下旬，苏珊失踪已经三个半月了。吉尔·莫利和我在曼哈顿中城。我们去拜访苏珊的治疗师玛丽·诺兰，她经常与舞女和妓女打交道。我们试图弄明白一件事。根据所有人的说法，苏珊在舞厅之外有很多发展的机会，而且她跳舞也赚不了多少钱，可她还是坚持做下去。

00:16:45.470 --> 00:17:21.960
<v Mary Nolan>Susan could not cut the ties with that world because it was a powerful pull for her. So something was happening. I guess the term would be repetition compulsion. It's acting out some type of an early event to get it right in the future. And she worked the whole gamut of the adult sex industry. I don't think she missed a wrinkle because she had a need to know and do this. And then she had a need to write about it and tell people about it.
<v Mary Nolan>苏珊无法切断与那个世界的联系，因为它对她有强大的吸引力。所以肯定有什么事情在发生。我想这个术语应该是“强迫性重复”。即把某种早期的事件重演，试图在未来将其纠正。她尝试了整个成人性产业的全部范围。我认为她没有错过任何环节，因为她有一种去了解和尝试的需要。然后她又有一种把这些写下来并告诉人们的需要。

00:17:21.960 --> 00:17:34.240
<v Man 2>And now a striptease from the beautiful Susan Walsh for you out there in Midnight Blue land.
<v Man 2>现在，美丽的苏珊·沃尔什为你献上一段脱衣舞。

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:50.270
<v Susan Walsh>Hi, I'm Susan Walsh and I'm a dancer. This is what I do for you when I dance in gentlemen's clubs. I move as if I were your lover, some fantastic embodiment of [? veloxed ?] beauty, breathless, hungry siren--
<v Susan Walsh>嗨，我是苏珊·沃尔什，我是一名舞者。当我在绅士俱乐部跳舞时，我为你做这些。我的动作仿佛我是你的情人，是某种奇幻美的化身，令人窒息的、饥渴的海妖——

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:58.800
<v Sandy Tolan>Susan wrote this essay for Al Goldstein's Midnight Blue porn cable show. And defending the notion of free speech, they put it on.
<v Sandy Tolan>苏珊为阿尔·戈德斯坦的“午夜蓝”色情有线电视节目写了这篇文章。为了捍卫言论自由，他们播出了。

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:06.250
<v Susan Walsh>Now I will be [UNINTELLIGIBLE] for you. You say you will, you must tease my sexual nerves.
<v Susan Walsh>现在我要为你……你说是你要的，你必须挑逗我的性神经。

00:18:06.250 --> 00:18:14.690
<v Susan Walsh>You laugh when I  struggle to protect my nipples from your raggedy fingers, as if I'm trying to believe the absurd notion that I'm real.
<v Susan Walsh>当你用粗糙的手指试图去碰我的乳头时，你笑了，就好像我试图相信自己是真实的这一荒谬想法一样。

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:21.620
<v Sandy Tolan>She smiles, takes off her top, calls the bar patrons, "Pathetic droplets of insect mucus."
<v Sandy Tolan>她微笑着脱掉上衣，称吧台顾客为“可悲的昆虫粘液滴”。

00:18:21.620 --> 00:18:38.320
<v Susan Walsh>We count the dollar bills you stuff into our costumes or fold into nauseatingly cute shapes like frogs or flowers. We unravel it all at the end of the night, our legs coated with dust and bruises and memories of your existence rush from our mind.
<v Susan Walsh>我们数着你塞进我们服装里的钞票，或者折成恶心可爱的青蛙或花朵形状。我们在深夜解开这一切，我们的腿上沾满灰尘、淤青和对你存在的记忆，这些从我们的脑海中飞逝。

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:51.660
<v Susan Walsh>If we thought about you too long, we'd go crazy. So we stuff your bills in our pockets, just like we stuff the idea that maybe we all lost out. Maybe paying the rent just isn't worth--
<v Susan Walsh>如果我们长时间想你，我们会疯掉的。所以我们把你的钞票塞进兜里，就像我们塞住那个想法：也许我们全都输了。也许付房租根本不值得——

00:18:51.660 --> 00:19:06.120
<v Sandy Tolan>Christmastime now, I'm back in New York. It's more than five months since anyone's heard a word from Susan. Susan's father, Floyd Merchant, drives in from New Jersey to see me. He looks like he's been crying. He says he often talked to Susan about quitting go-go.
<v Sandy Tolan>现在是圣诞节，我回到纽约。距离大家听到苏珊的消息已经过去五个多月了。苏珊的父亲弗洛伊德·麦钱特从新泽西开车来见我。他看起来像是哭过。他说他经常劝苏珊退出舞厅。

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:28.800
<v Floyd Merchant>The go-go bars were the worst place for somebody with their head on straight. Her's wasn't on straight. First of all, she's a recovering alcoholic and drug addict and is sitting on the railroad tracks jumping off every time the train passes. And then jumping right back on. I thought she might have cardiac arrest. I was almost sure she was going to go back to drinking and using.
<v Floyd Merchant>对于头脑清醒的人来说，舞厅是最糟糕的地方。而她的头脑并不清醒。首先，她是一个正在康复的酗酒者和吸毒者，却坐在铁轨上，每次火车经过就跳开。然后又跳回去。我以为她会心脏病发作。我几乎确定她会回去喝酒和吸毒。

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:45.670
<v Sandy Tolan>Susan's health was failing. She had emphysema, an ulcer, and chronic bronchitis. And then she did start drinking and using drugs again, mixing them with the anti-anxiety drug, Xanax. It was a potent cocktail and Susan started getting more and more disconnected from reality.
<v Sandy Tolan>苏珊的健康状况在恶化。她患有肺气肿、溃疡和慢性支气管炎。然后她确实又开始喝酒和吸毒，还将它们与抗焦虑药物阿普唑仑混合使用。这是一个强效的组合，苏珊开始越来越与现实脱节。

00:19:45.670 --> 00:20:08.640
<v Floyd Merchant>She was already living in a fantasy world, in a paranoid fantasy world. Not a happy fantasy world. She was running to people saying, there's a contract out on me, but don't tell anybody. Then she'd run to somebody else and say, there's a contract out on me, but don't tell anybody. And this is a preliminary to a real breakdown.
<v Floyd Merchant>她已经生活在一个幻想世界里，一个偏执的幻想世界里。不是快乐的幻想世界。她跑到人们面前说，有人给我下了合同，但别告诉任何人。然后她又跑到另一个人面前说，有人给我下了合同，但别告诉任何人。这是精神崩溃的前兆。

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:20.900
<v Melissa Hines>She was addicted to the fantasy part of her life. A lot of the people that she associated with from the bars and stuff like that, they played the fantasy of FBI and CIA.
<v Melissa Hines>她沉迷于她生活中的幻想部分。她从夜店结识的许多人，都扮演着FBI和CIA的幻想游戏。

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:28.240
<v Sandy Tolan>Now we're back in Jersey, Newark, on a windy, bitter December day. Jill and I are visiting Melissa Hines, Susan's best friend.
<v Sandy Tolan>现在我们回到了新泽西，纽瓦克，在一个风大刺骨的十二月天。吉尔和我去拜访苏珊最好的朋友梅丽莎·海因斯。

00:20:28.240 --> 00:21:01.840
<v Melissa Hines>She had a friend that claimed that he belonged to the CIA. He was playing the role that she wanted to hear. Oh, I'm CIA. I'm going to Washington for the weekend. Oh, I'm working undercover against the mafia. So it was like this big role playing stuff that I think she lived for that fantasy and the danger that she thought she was in. It was crazy.
<v Melissa Hines>她有个朋友声称他属于CIA。他扮演着她想听的角色。哦，我是CIA。我周末要去华盛顿。哦，我正在执行针对黑手党的卧底任务。所以就像是某种大型角色扮演，我认为她为那种幻想和她自以为身处的危险而活。太疯狂了。

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:05.700
<v Jill Morley>And what did the guy turn out to be?
<v Jill Morley>那个家伙后来被发现是什么人？

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:17.020
<v Melissa Hines>He turned out to be-- worked for a trucking company.
<v Melissa Hines>他被发现是……在一家货运公司工作。

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:37.300
<v Melissa Hines>But lot of the fantasy world that she lived in, I think it had a lot to do with the fact that she was once diagnosed with bipolar disorder, manic depressiveness, and she wasn't taking her medication. So she needed a lot of help.
<v Melissa Hines>但她所生活的幻想世界，我认为这和她曾经被诊断患有双相情感障碍、躁郁症有很大关系，而且她没有吃药。所以她需要很多帮助。

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:49.710
<v Sandy Tolan>Dozens of presents are piled up under Melissa's Christmas tree, most for her nine-month-old boy. Melissa's having a hard time talking to us. She and Susan used to celebrate Christmas together, and Susan was there when the baby was born.
<v Sandy Tolan>梅丽莎的圣诞树下堆满了礼物，大部分是给她九个月大的儿子的。梅丽莎很难跟我们交谈。她和苏珊过去常一起庆祝圣诞节，苏珊在她孩子出生时也在场。

00:21:49.710 --> 00:21:57.280
<v Sandy Tolan>Melissa gets up, turns on a light, retrieves a well-worn folder. Like everyone in Susan's life, Melissa's been trying to figure out what happened.
<v Sandy Tolan>梅丽莎起身，打开灯，取出一个磨损的文件夹。像苏珊生命中的每个人一样，梅丽莎一直试图弄清楚发生了什么。

00:21:57.280 --> 00:22:00.460
<v Melissa Hines>This is stuff that I wrote down.
<v Melissa Hines>这是我写下来的东西。

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.040
<v Sandy Tolan>What is it?
<v Sandy Tolan>是什么？

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:32.150
<v Melissa Hines>It's different people that'd seen her. I wrote down who was calling her. Who she was associating with. She was around a lot of different people. I mean, Friday, July 12, Susan went to Towne Tap in Irvington and was sick. I was at her house and I talked to her and I left. That was the last time I'd seen her, was July 12.
<v Melissa Hines>是不同见到她的人。我写下了谁在给她打电话。她和谁在一起。她身边有很多不同的人。我的意思是，7月12日星期五，苏珊去了欧文顿的Towne Tap，当时她病了。我在她家，我和她谈过话然后离开了。那是最后一次见到她，是在7月12日。

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:41.480
<v Melissa Hines>July 13, Susan worked at the Showplace from 5:30 at night to 1:45 AM.
<v Melissa Hines>7月13日，苏珊在表演场所工作，从晚上5点半到凌晨1点45分。

00:22:41.480 --> 00:22:50.470
<v Sandy Tolan>On July 16, Susan left her house around noon. By 3:30, Melissa had a strange feeling. She hurried over to Susan's.
<v Sandy Tolan>7月16日，苏珊中午左右离开家。到3点半，梅丽莎有了一种奇怪的感觉。她匆忙赶到苏珊家。

00:22:50.470 --> 00:23:11.270
<v Melissa Hines>I rung the bell and it looked like there was nobody there and nobody answered. And I got a very bad feeling. Just emptiness inside.
<v Melissa Hines>我按了门铃，看起来里面没人，也没人回应。我有一种非常糟糕的感觉。内心只有空虚。

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:51.100
<v Sandy Tolan>At first, everyone had a hunch. Susan had been murdered by a stalker. Susan had been kidnapped and sold to a motorcycle gang. Susan had been abducted by the Russian mob for sniffing around the story she and I were going to do. Susan was a streetwalker in Newark. She was a call girl in Elizabeth. A dancer in a nightclub upstate or she'd fallen in with a vampire cult. Or she'd checked herself into rehab. Or she enrolled in the witness protection plan. Or she'd died of a drug overdose. As time has passed, more and more of her friends, family, and coworkers have come to believe Susan Walsh is dead.
<v Sandy Tolan>起初，每个人都有预感。苏珊被一个跟踪狂谋杀了。苏珊被绑架并卖给了摩托车帮。苏珊因为调查我们打算做的那个故事而被俄罗斯黑手党绑架了。苏珊是纽瓦克的站街女。她是伊丽莎白的应召女郎。是州北部的舞厅舞女，或者她陷入了一个吸血鬼邪教。或者她自己进了康复中心。或者她加入了证人保护计划。或者她吸毒过量死亡了。随着时间的推移，越来越多的朋友、家人和同事开始相信苏珊·沃尔什已经死了。

00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:53.740
<v Jill Morley>Which Which house? Is it the one with the rolling Christmas lights?
<v Jill Morley>哪一栋房子？是挂着滚动圣诞灯的那一栋吗？

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:55.250
<v Sandy Tolan>No, I think it's this one.
<v Sandy Tolan>不，我想是这一栋。

00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:57.340
<v Jill Morley>Wait, let me just make sure.
<v Jill Morley>等一下，让我确认一下。

00:23:57.340 --> 00:24:22.540
<v Sandy Tolan>January. We look up a guy who says he thinks he knows what happened. He worked with Susan in the business. The guy says he'll talk on a couple of conditions. If we don't use his name, if we distort his voice, and if he talks just to Jill, not to me. She worked go-go, he feels she understands the life. Plus he clearly prefers the idea of a woman visiting him. I wait in the car.
<v Sandy Tolan>一月。我们找了一个声称他认为自己知道发生了什么事的家伙。他曾在这个行业和苏珊一起工作。这人说他会在几个条件下谈话。如果我们不用他的名字，如果我们对他的声音做变声处理，而且如果他只对吉尔谈，而不是对我。她做过舞厅，他觉得她懂这个生活。再说他显然更喜欢女性来访。我在车里等。

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:33.440
<v Jill Morley>OK. I'm a little nervous. Some dog's barking. Oh boy.
<v Jill Morley>好的。我有点紧张。有只狗在叫。哦，天哪。

00:24:33.440 --> 00:24:37.690
<v Jill Morley>Hey puppy. Man, it is cold out.
<v Jill Morley>嘿，小狗。天哪，外面真冷。

00:24:37.690 --> 00:24:44.040
<v Man 3>Star fleet command is waiting for my official report. [UNINTELLIGIBLE PHRASE].
<v Man 3>星际舰队指挥部正在等待我的正式报告。[听不清短语]。

00:24:44.040 --> 00:24:50.990
<v Man 3>Can I offer you a drink, like alcohol, wine? Gin and tonic? Anything like that?
<v Man 3>我可以给你倒杯酒吗，比如酒精，葡萄酒？金汤力？类似这种东西？

00:24:50.990 --> 00:25:13.400
<v Sandy Tolan>Here's what Jill reports from the interview. He lives with his invalid mother. Copies of Mentertainment, the guide to Jersey go-go, are scattered on the table. Nailed into the wall there's a whip broken in half. In his spare time, the guy makes knives. he keeps a photo album, Polaroids of his go-go girls to help him book clubs. He has 80 dancers working all over Jersey. He drives them to and from their gigs.
<v Sandy Tolan>这就是吉尔从采访中汇报的情况。他和残疾的母亲住在一起。桌上散落着《娱乐》，新泽西舞厅指南。墙上钉着一根折断的鞭子。闲暇时，这家伙制造刀具。他保存着相册，那些他旗下舞女的拍立得照片，方便他联系夜店。他在新泽西各地有80名舞女在工作。他负责接送她们去工作。

00:25:13.400 --> 00:25:34.560
<v Man 3>You're your own boss. It's your car. You can tell them to drink, smoke, or not. I constantly having girls say, well, can I smoke in here? And I'm like, yeah. No problem. But I got a little bit of the power there. I could tell them, no, suffer. Let's see you go through a nicotine fit for the next half hour. I'm sadistic.
<v Man 3>你是你自己的老板。这是你的车。你可以告诉她们可以喝酒、抽烟或者不行。经常有女孩说，好吧，我可以在这里抽烟吗？我就像，好吧。没问题。但我有一点权力在那里。我可以告诉她们，不，忍着。让我们看看你接下来半小时怎么应对尼古丁戒断反应。我是个虐待狂。

00:25:34.560 --> 00:25:37.190
<v Jill Morley>I guess so.
<v Jill Morley>我想是吧。

00:25:37.190 --> 00:25:46.070
<v Sandy Tolan>During the interview, the guy won't look Jill in the eyes. He turns on the TV, puts it on mute, stares at it. He puffs on his pipe, lighting it over and over.
<v Sandy Tolan>采访期间，这家伙不看吉尔的眼睛。他打开电视，静音，盯着屏幕。他抽着烟斗，一遍又一遍地点燃。

00:25:46.070 --> 00:25:50.980
<v Jill Morley>Let me ask you some more stuff about Susan. What kind of person was she?
<v Jill Morley>让我再问你一些关于苏珊的事情。她是什么样的人？

00:25:50.980 --> 00:26:05.820
<v Man 3>She is your typical, average dancer. If there was rap music on, she could dance to that. If it was rock and roll, she could dance to that. It didn't matter, she was good about the whole thing.
<v Man 3>她是你典型的、普通的舞女。如果放的是说唱音乐，她就能跳那个。如果是摇滚乐，她也能跳。没关系，她做得很不错。

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:24.650
<v Man 3>For somebody who was 36 and danced, I'd say she was in very good shape. She wasn't untoned or anything like that. She was pretty tight. The only thing she didn't have was a tan.
<v Man 3>对于一个36岁还在跳舞的人来说，我会说她状态非常好。她并不松垮或者类似的情况。她相当紧致。唯一没有的就是晒黑。

00:26:24.650 --> 00:26:26.100
<v Jill Morley>What do you think happened to her?
<v Jill Morley>你认为她发生了什么？

00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:46.150
<v Man 3>I think she fell in some sort of a fatal attraction who made her just that. And she got into somebody's car that she knew and drove away with him and never came back.
<v Man 3>我想她陷入了某种致命吸引，让她变成了那样。她上了某个她认识的人的车，然后和他一起离开了，就再也没回来。

00:26:46.150 --> 00:26:51.100
<v Jill Morley>What makes you think that, that it was a fatal attraction thing? Had you heard about this happening?
<v Jill Morley>是什么让你觉得是致命吸引的事？你听说过这种事吗？

00:26:51.100 --> 00:27:18.960
<v Man 3>Yeah, she had spoke to me within the prior two weeks to this and said how somebody was constantly beeping her. Susan can just be so friendly, so nice and naive. Maybe she didn't realize what kind of person this actually is.
<v Man 3>是的，她在出事前两周内曾跟我提起过，有人不断地给她的传呼机发信息。苏珊有时太友善、太好、太天真了。也许她没意识到这到底是个什么样的人。

00:27:18.960 --> 00:27:35.410
<v Sandy Tolan>It's not clear how much this go-go driver really knows, but Susan did tell people she had a stalker. She told me the week before she disappeared. She told Melissa. She told the therapist. And during a shoot for a documentary Jill's producing, she told a group of other dancers, two days before she disappeared.
<v Sandy Tolan>目前还不清楚这个舞厅司机到底知道多少，但苏珊确实告诉过别人她有个跟踪狂。她在失踪前一周告诉了我。她告诉了梅丽莎。她告诉了治疗师。而且在吉尔制作的一部纪录片拍摄过程中，她在失踪前两天告诉了一群其他舞女。

00:27:35.410 --> 00:27:40.700
<v Susan Walsh>That's my beeper. It's probably a stalker right now. I do have a stalker.
<v Susan Walsh>那是我的传呼机。现在可能就是跟踪狂。我确实有一个跟踪狂。

00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:41.330
<v Jill Morley>You You have a stalker?
<v Jill Morley>你……你有一个跟踪狂？

00:27:41.330 --> 00:27:42.630
<v Woman 3>I have a stalker too.
<v Woman 3>我也有一个跟踪狂。

00:27:42.630 --> 00:27:45.260
<v Susan Walsh>I have a stalker. I usually have stalkers.
<v Susan Walsh>我有一个跟踪狂。我通常都有跟踪狂。

00:27:45.260 --> 00:28:15.930
<v Sandy Tolan>It could have been Susan's paranoia talking. Most of the people who knew her well believe she died of a drug overdose and whoever was with the panicked and disposed of the body. And the Nutley, New Jersey, police say they checked out the stalker theory. They say they twice hauled in a guy and determined he had nothing to do with Susan's disappearance. But the cops, themselves, were slow in getting started. A week or so after Susan vanished, I called them to see what they knew. A detective told me, well, she's, you know, a dancer. She's probably out, you know, partying.
<v Sandy Tolan>这可能是苏珊的偏执妄想在作祟。大多数了解她的人认为她死于吸毒过量，而无论当时和谁在一起，那个人都惊慌失措并处理了尸体。新泽西州纳特利的警察说他们调查了跟踪狂理论。他们说他们两次传唤了一个家伙，确定他和苏珊的失踪无关。但警察自己起步很慢。苏珊失踪一周左右后，我打电话给他们看看他们知道什么。一位侦探告诉我，嗯，她，你知道，是个舞女。她可能出去，你知道，狂欢去了。

00:28:15.930 --> 00:28:24.790
<v Sandy Tolan>Eventually several of us pointed out Susan was also a journalist on assignment. Within days, they'd begun a major investigation.
<v Sandy Tolan>最终，我们中有几个人指出苏珊也是一位正在执行任务的记者。几天之内，他们就开始了一项重大调查。

00:28:24.790 --> 00:28:28.830
<v Sandy Tolan>Yeah, we wanted to see Detective Ryan. I'm Sandy Tolan. He's expecting us.
<v Sandy Tolan>是的，我们想见瑞安侦探。我是桑迪·托兰。他在等我们。

00:28:28.830 --> 00:28:42.090
<v Ira Glass>Jill and I finally got to talk to the cops in December. But before we could ask them any questions, they made a big point of showing us how much work they'd done. Hundreds of hours, three loose leaf binders filled up with information on the case.
<v Ira Glass>吉尔和我终于在十二月和警察谈上了。但在我们能问他们任何问题之前，他们特意向我们展示了他们做了多少工作。数百小时，三个装满案件信息的活页夹。

00:28:42.090 --> 00:28:57.400
<v Ira Glass>We sat down at a small round table with detectives Johnson and Ferraro. On the walls, framed posters from cop movies-- Out for Justice , One Good Cop. Detective Ferraro delivers the official line, "Nutley police believe Susan Walsh is still alive."
<v Ira Glass>我们和约翰逊及法拉罗侦探坐在一张圆桌旁。墙上挂着警匪片的剧照——《正义》，《好警察》。法拉罗侦探给出了官方说法：“纳特利警方认为苏珊·沃尔什还活着。”

00:28:57.400 --> 00:29:16.360
<v Detective Ferraro>It's just that she's chosen not to come home at this time. We don't have any other reasons to feel that through all the interviews that we've taken and statements that we've taken and people that we've talked to don't really have any concrete evidence to show something has happened to her.
<v Detective Ferraro>只是她目前选择不回家。通过我们所做的所有采访和陈述，以及我们谈话过的人，我们没有任何其他理由感到她已经发生了什么，没有具体证据。

00:29:16.360 --> 00:29:25.770
<v Sandy Tolan>Nutley police say they've checked out many reports of people who claim they saw Susan street walking in Newark, dancing go-go in North Jersey or New York. But nothing checked out.
<v Sandy Tolan>纳特利警方说他们核实了许多关于人们声称看到苏珊在纽瓦克站街、在新泽西北部或纽约跳舞的报告。但没有一条核实是真的。

00:29:25.770 --> 00:29:29.360
<v Detective Ferraro>Every lead dead-ended. There was just nothing else to go on.
<v Detective Ferraro>每条线索都是死胡同。根本没有其他进展。

00:29:29.360 --> 00:29:37.870
<v Sandy Tolan>And so the investigation petered out. Then in February, hopes rose again as Susan made prime time.
<v Sandy Tolan>于是调查陷入了停滞。然后在二月，苏珊登上了黄金时段，希望再次燃起。

00:29:37.870 --> 00:29:41.350
<v Man 4>Tonight on Unsolved Mysteries .
<v Man 4>今晚《未解之谜》。

00:29:41.350 --> 00:29:57.190
<v Unsolved Mysteries Host>Susan Walsh was a woman who lived on the edge, a stripper turned journalist whose chosen assignments plunged her into a hazardous stew of Russian mobsters and self-proclaimed vampires. In the end, however, Susan Walsh's walk on the wild side may have led to her death.
<v Unsolved Mysteries Host>苏珊·沃尔什是一个生活在边缘的女人，一个脱衣舞女转行的记者，她选择的采访任务使她陷入了由俄罗斯黑帮和自称吸血鬼的人组成的危险泥潭。然而最终，苏珊·沃尔什在狂野一面的漫步可能导致了她的死亡。

00:29:57.190 --> 00:30:10.490
<v Sandy Tolan>It was another false hope producing few new leads. Months before, Jim Ridgeway and I had watched them film part of the docudrama. It was in Tower Books where Jim and Susan had done a book signing for Red Light.
<v Sandy Tolan>这是另一个虚假的希望，几乎没产生什么新线索。几个月前，吉姆·里奇韦和我在塔图书店看他们拍摄部分纪实剧。那是吉姆和苏珊为《红灯》举行签售会的地方。

00:30:10.490 --> 00:30:14.540
<v Sandy Tolan>Now, the Unsolved Mysteries crew was shooting a reenactment.
<v Sandy Tolan>现在，《未解之谜》剧组正在拍摄重演。

00:30:14.540 --> 00:30:18.200
<v Man 5>Very quite please. This is rehearsal.
<v Man 5>请保持安静。这是彩排。

00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:26.890
<v Sandy Tolan>Up on the mezzanine there's wine, cheese, cameras, klieg lights, and actors playing the parts of Jim and Susan. Suddenly, the director spots the real Jim.
<v Sandy Tolan>二楼有酒、奶酪、摄像机、强力射灯，还有扮演吉姆和苏珊的演员。突然，导演发现了真正的吉姆。

00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:30.040
<v Producer>Hey, we got an impostor here. Get him out of here.
<v Producer>嘿，我们这儿有个冒牌货。让他出去。

00:30:30.040 --> 00:30:31.200
<v Woman 3>Hey, how you doing.
<v Woman 3>嘿，你好吗。

00:30:31.200 --> 00:30:36.670
<v Producer>What are you doing, you communist. Get over here. Get over to that corner. I'm serious. Come here. I can't have you in the shot. Come here.
<v Producer>你在干什么，你这个共产主义者。到这儿来。去那个角落。我是认真的。过来。我不能让你在镜头里。过来。

00:30:36.670 --> 00:30:46.470
<v Sandy Tolan>We stand in the corner, looking out at actors who look disturbingly like the real Jim Ridgeway-- tall, greying, paternal. And the real Susan Walsh-- slight, blond, vibrant.
<v Sandy Tolan>我们站在角落里，看着那些长得令人不安地像真正的吉姆·里奇韦——高大、灰发、慈祥——以及真正的苏珊·沃尔什——苗条、金发、充满活力——的演员。

00:30:46.470 --> 00:30:48.150
<v Man 5>Step back please.
<v Man 5>请退后。

00:30:48.150 --> 00:30:49.620
<v Man 6>Move your lights.
<v Man 6>移开你们的灯。

00:30:49.620 --> 00:30:57.280
<v Man 5>OK, this is picture. Everyone this is picture. Stand by. Roll sound. We're rolling.
<v Man 5>好，这是画面。大家注意这是画面。准备。录音。开始录制。

00:30:57.280 --> 00:31:01.080
<v Woman 4>[UNINTELLIGIBLE]. Take one. Mark.
<v Woman 4>[听不清]。第一条。打板。

00:31:01.080 --> 00:31:02.980
<v Producer>And action.
<v Producer>开始。

00:31:02.980 --> 00:31:07.600
<v Actress>[UNINTELLIGIBLE]. Hi. You came out again for us--
<v Actress>[听不清]。嗨。你又为我们出来了——

00:31:07.600 --> 00:31:26.450
<v Sandy Tolan>The fake Susan makes small talk, signing copies of Red Light while the fake Jim stands by. I point to the fake Jim's larger belly and make a face. Ridgeway obliges with a sour grin, but he's looking past me, gazing at the image of a woman he worked with for three years, alive again for a moment.
<v Sandy Tolan>冒牌苏珊在寒暄，在签售《红灯》的同时，冒牌吉姆站在一边。我指着冒牌吉姆更突出的肚子，做了个鬼脸。里奇韦配合地露出苦笑，但他看向我身后，凝视着一个他合作了三年的女人的图像，她仿佛又活了过来。

00:31:26.450 --> 00:31:26.940
<v Producer>And cut.
<v Producer>卡。

00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:32.860
<v Man 5>And cut. That's a cut. Back to one everyone, please. Back to one. Thank you
<v Man 5>卡。卡了。大家回到位置，拜托。回到位置。谢谢。

00:31:32.860 --> 00:31:38.490
<v Susan Walsh>I've stayed in it so long that my health is so bad. I have emphysema, bronchitis, and an ulcer.
<v Susan Walsh>我干太久了，导致身体很差。我有肺气肿、支气管炎和溃疡。

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:38.850
<v Woman 5>Geez.
<v Woman 5>天哪。

00:31:38.850 --> 00:31:42.660
<v Susan Walsh>Yeah, and I was in the hospital twice in the last two weeks.
<v Susan Walsh>是的，过去两周我进了两次医院。

00:31:42.660 --> 00:31:52.840
<v Sandy Tolan>This is the real Susan in the documentary shoot with Jill and the other dancers. It was two days before she disappeared and it was like Susan was watching herself go down.
<v Sandy Tolan>这是真正的苏珊在吉尔和舞女们的纪录片拍摄现场。那是在她失踪前两天，感觉就像苏珊在看着自己一步步坠落。

00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:54.320
<v Woman 6>I just went through the same thing.
<v Woman 6>我刚刚经历了一样的事情。

