00:45:42.710 --> 00:45:52.480
<v Joy Gregory>"Must be tiring having to think that. You can never really let down your guard. Have you ever cried in front of someone to show that you're scared, upset?"
<v Joy Gregory>“那样想一定很累吧。你永远不能真正放下防备。你在别人面前哭过，展现出你的恐惧和不安吗？”

00:45:52.480 --> 00:46:03.310
<v Joy Gregory>George didn't say anything. A long silence settled between as. We were a cut cord, a swarm of static.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治什么也没说。漫长的沉默在我们之间定格。我们是一条断了的绳子，是一阵静电。

00:46:03.310 --> 00:46:21.960
<v Joy Gregory>"What's going on, George? Why is it unsafe to feel anything but defensiveness or violence in this office? Do you think I'm going to take advantage of you?" Immediately I realized I'd made a blunder by allowing him the opportunity to sexualize our interaction.
<v Joy Gregory>“到底怎么了，乔治？为什么在这间办公室里，除了防御或暴力，其他什么感受都是不安全的？你觉得我会利用你吗？”我立刻意识到我犯了一个错误，让他有机会将我们的互动性化了。

00:46:21.960 --> 00:46:50.630
<v Joy Gregory>"You, take advantage of me? Isn't that supposed to be the other way around?" He leaned back in his chair, lit another cigarette. I saw the smoke slide from his mouth, felt it wrap around me in a blue and gauzy cloud, decking me in the moving material of a see-through dress.
<v Joy Gregory>“你，利用我？难道不应该是反过来的吗？”他靠在椅子上，点燃了另一支烟。我看着烟雾从他嘴里滑出，感到它像一团蓝色且薄如纱的云一样包裹着我，给我穿上了一件透视裙。

00:46:50.630 --> 00:47:00.870
<v Joy Gregory>George believed that the bodies outside him were missiles, poised and poisonous. His aggressive, slit-eyed stance is a typically male phenomenon.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治相信他外部的身体是导弹，蓄势待发且充满毒性。他那种攻击性的、眯着眼的立场是一种典型的男性现象。

00:47:00.870 --> 00:47:09.790
<v Joy Gregory>My eating disorder, the obsessive desire to be thin, thin, thin, and perfectly, poisonously poised is typically a female phenomenon.
<v Joy Gregory>我的饮食失调，那种想变得瘦、瘦、瘦，并且完美地、毒性地保持平衡的强迫欲望，则是典型的女性现象。

00:47:09.790 --> 00:47:47.590
<v Joy Gregory>George and I were both victims of our culture's fear of the feminine, unable to lay down our system of weapons and spread our legs open to life because we learned that in this posture, we will be shamed not invigorated. We did not know how to trust what we could not dominate. And the recovering anorexic is not only in a particularly good position to articulate these truths, she is also ironically, in a particularly good position-- vis-a-vis therapy-- to treat the misogynist male. She understands, perhaps better than anyone, the urge to whip and dominate, discipline and even delete the female form.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治和我都是文化对女性恐惧的受害者，无法放下我们的武器系统并向生活敞开双腿，因为我们学到在这种姿态下，我们会感到羞耻而不是活力。我们不知道如何信任我们无法统治的东西。而一个康复中的厌食症患者不仅处于阐述这些真相的特别位置，而且具有讽刺意味的是，在心理治疗方面，她也处于治疗厌女男性的特别位置。她或许比任何人都理解鞭笞、统治、管教甚至删除女性形态的冲动。

00:47:47.590 --> 00:48:11.690
<v Joy Gregory>For years, I was hungry but could not risk the softness of surrender. I dreamt of letting down my guard, sitting at a table on which silver dishes steamed and ingesting colors. Orange carrots, the soft wombs of tomatoes, the tangy dirt of chocolate cake. But I couldn't dare, couldn't trust enough to let myself go.
<v Joy Gregory>多年来，我一直感到饥饿，却不敢冒放弃抵抗的柔软风险。我梦想着放下防备，坐在摆满冒着热气银盘的桌子前，吞咽颜色。橙色的胡萝卜，番茄柔软的子宫，巧克力蛋糕那刺激的泥土气息。但我不敢，无法足够信任去让自己放手。

00:48:11.690 --> 00:48:22.500
<v Joy Gregory>These are the memories that came to mind when I looked at George, rigid in his chair, his face set against the seepage of any emotion that wasn't cruel or lewd.
<v Joy Gregory>当我看着乔治坐在椅子上僵硬着，他的脸抵御着任何非残忍或淫秽情感的渗入时，这些记忆涌上心头。

00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:43.320
<v Joy Gregory>He told me about forcing himself to rise before dawn each morning, working out two hours a day, jogging barefoot in the snow. I nodded yes, having done the same to myself.
<v Joy Gregory>他告诉我他强迫自己每天黎明前起床，每天锻炼两小时，在雪地里赤脚慢跑。我点头表示理解，因为我也对自己做过同样的事。

00:48:43.320 --> 00:49:02.930
<v Joy Gregory>The more deeply I went into it with him, the more difficult he became. Our therapy started to evolve, so that I played a mostly silent role, while he went on and on, endlessly it seemed. About Joanne's anatomy, the six hour plow, her tight little sex.
<v Joy Gregory>我和他的治疗越深入，他就变得越困难。我们的治疗开始演变，我扮演了一个大多时候保持沉默的角色，而他似乎无休止地继续谈论。谈论乔安娜的解剖结构，六小时的征服，她紧致的小性器官。

00:49:02.930 --> 00:49:29.880
<v Joy Gregory>What about me, I wanted to say to him. Does it occur to you that I'm a woman here? That you just might be offending me? And beneath that another smaller voice was crying, what about me? Am I not also attractive? Do I not measure up to your standards? Why not?
<v Joy Gregory>那我呢，我真想对他吼道。你意识到我是一个女人吗？你可能会冒犯到我吗？在那之下，另一个更小的声音在哭喊，那我呢？我不也很有吸引力吗？我不符合你的标准吗？为什么不？

00:49:29.880 --> 00:50:02.020
<v Joy Gregory>I began to realize our sessions were a lot like porn, in which I, the silent subject, absorbed his fantasies, and in my featurelessness, reflected them back to him. George let me know clearly what my role in our relationship was by shifting impatiently whenever I spoke. By the quick brushing motions he made with his hands as though to sweep away my words. By interrupting me and then exploding into a tyrannical temper if I asserted my right to finish my own sentence.
<v Joy Gregory>我开始意识到我们的会谈很像色情作品，我作为一个沉默的对象，吸收了他的幻想，并在我毫无特征的情况下将它们反射回给他。乔治通过我说话时焦躁地挪动身体，或者通过他用手快速刷动的动作（仿佛要扫掉我的话）来明确让我知道我在我们关系中的角色。通过打断我，然后在如果我坚持自己说完句子的权利时爆发成专制的脾气。

00:50:02.020 --> 00:50:05.090
<v Joy Gregory>"Quiet," he once roared at me.
<v Joy Gregory>“闭嘴，”他有一次对我怒吼。

00:50:05.090 --> 00:50:18.410
<v Joy Gregory>And I, like a little girl, sank back down in my seat, and felt darkness grow up around me.
<v Joy Gregory>而我，像个小女孩一样，缩回座位里，感觉到黑暗在我周围滋生。

00:50:18.410 --> 00:50:29.560
<v Joy Gregory>"I wonder if you ever think," I finally burst out to him one day, "That I might be uncomfortable with your sexual talk, with the kinds of expressions you use."
<v Joy Gregory>“我不知道你是否想过，”终于有一天我对他爆发道，“我可能对你的性谈话、你使用的表达方式感到不舒服。”

00:50:29.560 --> 00:50:36.430
<v Joy Gregory>"But you're a shrink," George said to me. "That's what you're here for. That's your whole job."
<v Joy Gregory>“但你是心理医生，”乔治对我说。“这就是你在这里的原因。这就是你的全部工作。”

00:50:36.430 --> 00:50:48.390
<v Joy Gregory>I wanted to reach out and slap him. "Not even in my office am I just a shrink. I am also a woman and the way you talk about my gender disgusts me."
<v Joy Gregory>我想伸手扇他一巴掌。“即使在我的办公室里，我也不仅仅是个心理医生。我还是一个女人，你谈论我性别的方式让我感到厌恶。”

00:50:48.390 --> 00:50:55.240
<v Joy Gregory>"I wouldn't ever talk to a woman I was trying to make it with like that, but you're not supposed to--"
<v Joy Gregory>“我绝不会那样和我想搞定的女人说话，但你不应该是……”

00:50:55.240 --> 00:50:57.740
<v Joy Gregory>"Supposed to what?"
<v Joy Gregory>“应该什么？”

00:50:57.740 --> 00:51:00.140
<v Joy Gregory>George looked uncomfortable.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治看起来很不自在。

00:51:00.140 --> 00:51:03.150
<v Joy Gregory>Halla-[BLEEP]-lujah, I thought.
<v Joy Gregory>哈利路亚，我想。

00:51:03.150 --> 00:51:06.030
<v Joy Gregory>"Supposed to mind," he said.
<v Joy Gregory>“不应该在意，”他说。

00:51:06.030 --> 00:51:09.740
<v Joy Gregory>"Surprise," I said. "I mind."
<v Joy Gregory>“惊喜，”我说。“我在意。”

00:51:09.740 --> 00:51:39.260
<v Joy Gregory>George looked up at me, his expression confused. My face felt all red. For one moment then, our masks dropped away. I could tell by the way George was looking at me that he was, for maybe the first time, considering me not as a function, but as a feeling. I smiled at him. He nodded, hello.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治看着我，表情困惑。我的脸感到一阵通红。就在那一刻，我们的面具掉落了。从乔治看我的方式，我看得出他大概是第一次没有把我当作一种功能，而是作为一个有感受的人在看待。我对他笑了。他点头，哈喽。

00:51:39.260 --> 00:51:53.800
<v Joy Gregory>Shortly after this encounter, George left the state for six weeks to do a series of carpentry jobs in Arizona. He returned to therapy in late May. He slumped down in his seat, looked at his lap.
<v Joy Gregory>这次接触后不久，乔治离开该州六周去亚利桑那州做一系列木工工作。五月下旬他回到治疗中。他瘫坐在座位上，看着自己的大腿。

00:51:53.800 --> 00:52:01.340
<v Joy Gregory>"I was going to call you," he said in a low voice. I'd never heard him use that voice before.
<v Joy Gregory>“我本来想给你打电话，”他低声说。我以前从未听过他用那种声音说话。

00:52:01.340 --> 00:52:03.820
<v Joy Gregory>"What happened?" I asked.
<v Joy Gregory>“发生了什么？”我问。

00:52:03.820 --> 00:52:26.900
<v Joy Gregory>"She left me," George said. He shook his head. "Just like that. I called her at her parents and she says it's completely finished. Gonzo. But I'm chasing her. I'm running after her like a goddamn desperate dog. Phoning her 10, 20 times a day, bawling in her ear. It doesn't matter what I do."
<v Joy Gregory>“她离开了我，”乔治说。他摇了摇头。“就这样。我给她父母打电话，她说一切都结束了。彻底完了。但我还在追她。我像条该死的绝望的狗一样跑着追她。一天给她打十、二十次电话，在她耳边哭。我做什么都没用。”

00:52:26.900 --> 00:52:32.600
<v Joy Gregory>"It doesn't matter what you do," I said. "Tell me more about that."
<v Joy Gregory>“无论你做什么都没用，”我说。“再多跟我说说。”

00:52:32.600 --> 00:52:36.840
<v Joy Gregory>"I've been trying every ploy with this bitch for the past week and I'm--"
<v Joy Gregory>“过去一周我试了所有手段来对付这个婊子，而且我……”

00:52:36.840 --> 00:52:40.850
<v Joy Gregory>"What? You're what?"
<v Joy Gregory>“什么？你是什么？”

00:52:40.850 --> 00:52:47.630
<v Joy Gregory>"Helpless." His mouth was a bitter line of tension, but his eyes were wet.
<v Joy Gregory>“无助。”他的嘴唇是一条紧张的苦涩线条，但他的眼睛湿润了。

00:52:47.630 --> 00:52:56.570
<v Joy Gregory>"I think that's what upsets you the most about Joanne's leaving. That you have no control. That you feel helpless to get her back."
<v Joy Gregory>“我想这就是乔安娜离开让你最难过的原因。因为你失去了控制。因为你感到无力挽回她。”

00:52:56.570 --> 00:53:18.580
<v Joy Gregory>George, to my surprise, nodded in agreement. His own pain had made him flexible, open to vision and suggestion. For the first time in six months of treatment, I think we really talked.
<v Joy Gregory>令我惊讶的是，乔治点头表示同意。他自己的痛苦让他变得灵活，对视角和建议开放。在六个月的治疗中，我认为我们第一次真正进行了交谈。

00:53:18.580 --> 00:53:39.200
<v Joy Gregory>The next few weeks brought some changes in George. He found himself facing an emotion he could not defend himself against. No amount of swearing or swaggering could express mourning. The pain of Joanne's leaving so suddenly broke his shield with an intensity neither of us had anticipated.
<v Joy Gregory>接下来的几周给乔治带来了一些改变。他发现自己面对一种他无法防御的情绪。任何咒骂或吹嘘都无法表达哀悼。乔安娜突然离去的痛苦以我们两人都没预料到的强度打破了他的盾牌。

00:53:39.200 --> 00:54:00.990
<v Joy Gregory>I was drawn into George now and I told him so. In some moments I think I saw his real face, the flow of emotion across it like wind working on sand. And I grew to love him and love the strength in his slow surrender.
<v Joy Gregory>我被乔治吸引住了，我告诉了他。在某些时刻，我想我看到了他真实的脸，情绪像风在沙地上掠过一样在上面流动。我开始爱他，并爱他在缓慢投降中的力量。

00:54:00.990 --> 00:54:11.490
<v Joy Gregory>It is August. I am 23 years old. I have never met George. I am just out of college. I weigh 88 pounds.
<v Joy Gregory>现在是八月。我23岁。我从未见过乔治。我刚大学毕业。我体重88磅。

00:54:11.490 --> 00:54:29.130
<v Joy Gregory>When I look out my bedroom window, I can see tulips. They are the most trusting beings. They with their throats always open. Their long gold tongues hanging out. Nothing bad happens to them. The sun doesn't rape them. They don't gag on the rain.
<v Joy Gregory>当我看向卧室窗外时，我能看到郁金香。它们是最信任的存在。它们的喉咙总是张开的。它们长长的金舌头伸出来。没有什么坏事发生在它们身上。太阳没有强奸它们。它们不会被雨水噎住。

00:54:29.130 --> 00:54:41.740
<v Joy Gregory>This day is really many months. I watch the world. I watch the natural cycle of things. Cliche as it may be, this is what cures me.
<v Joy Gregory>这一天其实持续了几个月。我观察这个世界。我观察事物的自然循环。尽管这很老套，但这就是治愈我的东西。

00:54:41.740 --> 00:54:58.430
<v Joy Gregory>There comes a moment when recovery is religious. When a person says, all right, I will have faith. I will lay down my sword and shield and see what the world works in me.
<v Joy Gregory>当康复成为一种宗教时，有一个时刻会到来。当一个人说，好吧，我会拥有信仰。我会放下我的剑和盾，看看世界在我身上起什么作用。

00:54:58.430 --> 00:55:30.690
<v Joy Gregory>I look away from my bedroom window and go downstairs, out onto the porch. Someone has set a table for me. Sliced strawberries lie like the tongues of maidens on a platter, wedges of cheese and bread. I put food in my mouth. For the first time in years, I swallow the softness of ice cream. I want to see if my body will blow up in disgusting fatness with this slow animal stupidity swelling in my stomach. It doesn't.
<v Joy Gregory>我从卧室窗户转过头，下楼来到门廊。有人为我摆好了桌子。切好的草莓像处女的舌头一样躺在盘子里，还有奶酪和面包。我把食物放进嘴里。多年来第一次，我吞咽下冰淇淋的柔软。我想看看我的身体是否会因为这种胃部膨胀的缓慢动物般的愚蠢而爆炸成恶心的肥胖。并没有。

00:55:30.690 --> 00:56:02.920
<v Joy Gregory>Letting down my guard, opening my many mouths does not bring about the ruin, the rape I had feared. On the contrary, food brings vitality back to me. I feel my hair take on its sheen, grow longer as though new stalks of thought are springing from my brain. My brain, now nourished, thinks in colors instead of calories. I can run harder. My eyes are moist enough to cry.
<v Joy Gregory>放下防备，张开我众多的嘴，并没有带来我所恐惧的毁灭和强奸。相反，食物带回了我的活力。我感到头发恢复了光泽，长长了，仿佛新的思想之茎正从大脑中萌芽。我的大脑，现在得到滋养，以颜色而不是卡路里思考。我能跑得更快。我的眼睛湿润到足以流泪。

00:56:02.920 --> 00:56:30.150
<v Joy Gregory>George started to taste-- styles, voices, times. He reported allowing himself to sleep late one morning. He started going out some night without his leather vest or black boots. Tried kissing a woman on the neck and going no farther. He brought wood home with him at the end of working days, stayed up late making small objects without any obvious functions. A box, a mobile, a chiseled plaque.
<v Joy Gregory>乔治开始品味——风格、声音、时间。他汇报说某天早上允许自己睡懒觉。他开始在某些晚上不穿皮背心或黑靴子出门。尝试亲吻女人的脖子但不再进一步。他工作日结束时带木头回家，熬夜制作一些没有明显功能的小物件。一个盒子，一个风铃，一块雕刻的牌匾。

00:56:30.150 --> 00:56:39.890
<v Joy Gregory>One day, he came to session and told me he had met a woman, [? Blucky, ?] whom he thought he could fall in love with if only he could get over Joanne.
<v Joy Gregory>有一天，他来会谈，告诉我他遇见了一个女人，布鲁基，他认为如果能走出乔安娜的影响，他可能会爱上她。

00:56:39.890 --> 00:57:01.280
<v Joy Gregory>"The other problem is," George said. "She's the greatest person but she's heavy. Maybe 30 pounds overweight. I've never made it with a fat woman before. You know me, I'm used to perfect curves. Thighs I can grab a hold of, someone I can flip like a doll." He gave me one of his lewd George smiles.
<v Joy Gregory>“另一个问题是，”乔治说。“她是个最好的人，但她很胖。可能超重30磅。我以前从没和胖女人做过。你知道我，我习惯了完美的曲线。我可以抓住的大腿，我可以像洋娃娃一样翻转的人。”他给了我一个乔治式的淫秽微笑。

00:57:01.280 --> 00:57:12.170
<v Joy Gregory>I was enchanted by the idea of George with a fat woman. I had seen enough of George changed, naked, to imagine how his body would be within a fat woman's arms.
<v Joy Gregory>我被乔治和一个胖女人在一起的想法所迷住。我已经足够多地看到改变后的、裸露的乔治，想象他身体在胖女人怀抱中的样子。

00:57:12.170 --> 00:57:54.290
<v Joy Gregory>I imagined her rocking him and him kissing her face and mouth. I could not help but see her spread legs on a bed and he, a little cowed by the site of so much, trying to touch her, allowing himself entry into the many layers of her life. He brushes her, goes up past her hip, until he touches the curved rib bone, the hard male bone taken a long time ago from the man buried and found only in the full woman's body.
<v Joy Gregory>我想象她摇晃着他，他亲吻她的脸和嘴。我不禁看到她分张的双腿在床上，而他，被如此多的景象吓到，试图触碰她，允许自己进入她生命的许多层面。他擦过她，越过她的臀部，直到碰到弯曲的肋骨，那个早已从被埋葬的男人身上取走，只在丰满女性身体中找到的坚硬雄性骨头。

00:57:54.290 --> 00:58:00.440
<v Ira Glass>Lauren Slater's story, "Striptease," was first published in the quarterly New Letters . It was read by actress Joy Gregory.
<v Ira Glass>劳伦·斯莱特的故事《脱衣舞》首次发表在季刊《新信》上。由演员乔伊·格雷戈里朗读。

